# The build context is exactly what the Dockerfiles' COPY lines read, and nothing else: everything
# is left out, then each COPY source of every Dockerfile in the repository is let back in.
# tests/test_dockerignore.py parses every Dockerfile and fails if a COPY source is left out here.
*
!requirements.lock
!tools/install_pinned.py
!src/
!LICENSE
!config/container.json
!deploy/fly/public.json
# Byte-code and an editable install's metadata are never part of an image, even inside src/.
**/__pycache__/
**/*.pyc
**/*.egg-info/
